 45	
 46	V1 proved the focus loop. The next slice turns the expanded Island into a
 47	truthful cross-session activity surface without giving it mutation authority.
 48	This section is binding for Phase 2A.
 49	
 50	### Authoritative sources
 51	
 52	Use the daemon's existing global snapshots:
 53	
 54	- `GET /v1/requests` for queued, running, waiting-for-permission, cancelling,
 55	  and errored request state across sessions.
 56	- `GET /v1/permissions` for currently pending permissions and their
 57	  request/session/tool/reason metadata.
 58	- `GET /v1/agent/sessions` remains the title/project/path lookup catalogue.
 59	
 60	Poll the two attention snapshots every three seconds while the Tauri Island is
 61	mounted, refresh immediately on mount and overlay open, and retain the last
 62	good snapshot if one request fails. This is an interim read-only projection,
 63	not a new runtime store. A unified replayable daemon attention stream remains
 64	the later target.
 65	
 66	Never infer running, blocked, failed, or complete state from session timestamps.
 67	Timestamps may order authoritative items; they may not create them.
 68	
 69	### Projection rules
 70	
 71	Project the snapshot into these display states:
 72	
 73	- `NeedsHuman`: every pending permission; de-duplicate its matching
 74	  `waiting_for_permission` request.
 75	- `Running`: queued or running requests.
 76	- `Cancelling`: cancelling requests.
 77	- `Failed`: the three newest errored requests in the current daemon registry.
 78	- Omit completed and cancelled requests.
 79	
 80	Join `session_id` to the fetched session catalogue for title/project display.
 81	Use a short session id fallback when the catalogue has not caught up. Do not
 82	render raw permission `args` in the Island; the existing transcript-adjacent
 83	permission surface remains the detail/action authority.
 84	
 85	### Compact-state priority
 86	
 87	The closed chip preserves the focused session title. Its trailing status reads,
 88	in priority order:
 89	
 90	1. `<n> need attention`
 91	2. `<n> running`
 92	3. existing `<n> recent`
 93	
 94	The dot uses `--warn` for human attention, the existing live accent for running,
 95	and the normal/empty treatment otherwise. No pulse or decorative animation.
 96	The accessible label and one polite live region announce the same factual count.
 97	
 98	### Expanded interaction
 99	
100	The popover remains one dialog and one material surface. When activity exists,
101	render an `Activity` section between search and session results:
102	
103	- needs-human items first, then failed, cancelling, and running;
104	- one plain summary row per item, with state, session title, and concise detail;
105	- clicking or pressing Enter on a summary toggles its inline disclosure;
106	- the disclosure may show project, tool/request state, and bounded reason;
107	- one ghost `Open session` action focuses the associated session through
108	  `Daemon::switch_session(id, title)` and closes the Island.
109	
110	Attention controls participate in a real Tab focus trap. Arrow-key/
111	`aria-activedescendant` session navigation remains scoped to the search input,
112	so using a disclosure button can never accidentally switch the selected session.
113	Escape still closes exactly one surface and restores the invoking focus.
114	
115	### Explicit Phase 2A deferrals
116	
117	- no approve/deny inside the Island;
118	- no inline reply/resume or stop action;
119	- no local dismiss/read state;
120	- no raw permission arguments;
121	- no browser, CI, GitHub, room, or Council cards;
122	- no claim that the polling projection is durable attention history.
123	
124	Those mutations follow only after the read-only state and ordering prove useful
125	and their daemon authorization contracts are explicit.
126	
127	## Existing foundations to reuse
128	
129	Do not recreate these systems:
130	
131	| Existing implementation | Reuse in Island work |
132	| --- | --- |
133	| `Daemon::sessions: RwSignal<Vec<SessionSummary>>` | search corpus and list data |
134	| `Daemon::session_id: RwSignal<Option<String>>` | focused-session identity |
135	| `Daemon::switch_session(id, title)` | sole session focus/switch operation |
136	| `sessions.rs::split_origin`, `fmt_relative_time`, `session_root`, project lookup | display metadata and normalized search text |
137	| `palette.rs::fuzzy_score` behavior | fuzzy scoring semantics; extract/move to a shared search helper rather than copy it |
138	| `PaletteView` keyboard pattern | input autofocus, ArrowUp/Down, Enter, Escape, backdrop click |
139	| `app.rs` `window_event_listener(ev::keydown, ...)` | `⌘P` global shortcut and overlay Escape priority |
140	| `host::running_in_tauri()` | mount/gating boundary |
141	| `styles/chrome.css` titlebar model | titlebar position and drag-region rules |
142	
143	Important fact: today `Daemon::switch_session` replaces the active transcript
144	and reconnects its SSE/permission streams. The Island must call it; it must not
145	attempt a second transcript/session runtime of its own.
146	
147	## User-facing model
148	
149	### Terminology
150	
  1	/* Dynamic Island — native titlebar session focus/search. Tauri-only in the
  2	   component tree; these selectors remain inert on web and extension hosts. */
  3	
  4	:root {
  5	  --island-max-w: 520px;
  6	  --island-popover-w: min(560px, calc(100vw - 32px));
  7	  --island-top: 64px;
  8	}
  9	
 10	.ocean-header {
 11	  position: relative;
 12	}
 13	
 14	.ocean-header__left {
 15	  display: flex;
 16	  align-items: center;
 17	  min-width: 0;
 18	}
 19	
 20	/* Center inside the real header/content column without transform. Fixed
 21	   descendants therefore stay viewport-fixed instead of inheriting a new
 22	   containing block. The percentage cap reserves both titlebar control zones. */
 23	.island-host {
 24	  position: absolute;
 25	  inset-inline: 0;
 26	  top: 11px;
 27	  width: min(var(--island-max-w), 44%);
 28	  height: var(--ctl-h);
 29	  margin-inline: auto;
 30	  z-index: 122;
 31	}
